== Problem description ==
Poco X3 and X3 Pro presents with severe system failures such as no power, non-functional cameras, and no audio output. In many cases, the device appears completely dead or fails to boot properly.

When powered via a DC power supply, the phone draws ~0.150 A after a boot prompt and then stalls, indicating that the CPU is attempting to initialize but fails shortly after.

This is a well-known defect on the Poco X3 Pro and is caused by CPU solder joint failure due to thermal stress and board flex.
[[File:Camera-not-working-poco.webp|thumb|Poco X3 (Figure 1) -- Camera not working even after replacing with known good parts]]

== Symptoms ==

* No audio (speaker, earpiece, microphone all dead)
* Rear and front cameras not detected / not working
* Device does not power on
* Black screen, no vibration
* Stuck at ~0.150 A on DCPS after pressing power
* No further current ramp (no boot)
* Issue persists after:
** Replacing battery
** Replacing screen
** Replacing cameras or audio components

== Solution ==
[[File:X3-pro-cpu.png|thumb|Poco X3 Pro (Figure 2) -- CPU location]]
[[File:X3-pro-cpu-reballed.png|thumb|Poco X3 Pro CPU (Figure 3) -- CPU reballed]]

=== Diagnostic Steps ===

# Connect device to DCPS
# Press power button
# Observe current behavior:
#* ~0.150 A stall confirms CPU fault
# Confirm no shorts on main power rails
# Rule out:
#* PMIC failure
#* Battery fault
#* Display fault

Once these are ruled out, proceed with CPU repair.
----

=== Repair Steps ===

# Remove logic board from device
# Shield surrounding components
# Preheat board evenly to avoid warping
# Remove CPU using controlled hot air
# Clean CPU pads and board pads thoroughly
# Reball CPU with correct solder size
# Inspect balls under microscope
# Reinstall CPU carefully aligned
# Reflow evenly and allow to cool naturally
# Clean flux residue